Last week, I had you write a multiply function in JavaScript which will produce the following outputs when invoked:
console.log(mul(2)(3)(4)); // output: 24 
console.log(mul(4)(3)(4)); // output: 48
Here's my solution:
function mul(a) {
 return function(b) {
 return function(c) {
 return a*b*c;
 }
 };
}
